[NARRATIVE]
UID: NAR-MECHANISM-MOOD-REVIEW
TITLE: The mechanism mood test: which mechanisms were rules or observations, and which are held for a ruling
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
WIDGET: prose
STATEMENT: >>>
Every node born as a MECHANISM was sorted on 2026-08-30 by the definition
grid's test ([LINK: DEC-NODE-FAMILIES]): if the world did something this
node says it does not, would you fix the world -- a rule, which can be
violated -- or fix the node -- a description, which can only be wrong? And
does it speak of every case, or record one observation? Ten classifiers
sorted 135 nodes; a second opinion argued both sides of every proposed
retype. 27 were retyped in place, keeping their UIDs
([LINK: DEC-UID-OUTLIVES-TYPE]); 4 are held at low confidence for
the operator, each wanting a split into a rule and a design rather than a
retype; 104 stayed mechanisms. The ledger is
[LINK: EV-GRID-MIGRATION-LEDGER]. Nothing here is signed; a verdict is the
test's reading, recorded in each node's NOTES.
<<<
PARENT_FP: >>>
DEC-NODE-FAMILIES:0000000
DEC-UID-OUTLIVES-TYPE:0000000
<<<
